WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:04.240
In a world still reeling from the impacts of Covid

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:08.640
we realise that this is a difficult&nbsp;
time for many people here.  

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.760
Fortunately, our economy has&nbsp;
fared much better than expected,

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.960
especially compared with
other parts of New Zealand.
 

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:23.280
This is largely because of our proximity to&nbsp;
Christchurch, our low reliance on tourism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:28.480
and residents shopping and supporting local.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:34.880
However, we’re not out of the woods yet, and the Council&nbsp;
would like help the community recover by:

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:38.365
Keeping rates as low as possible 

00:00:38.365 --> 00:00:42.000
Supporting existing and new businesses

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.496
Marketing Waimakariri as&nbsp;
destination for domestic visitors

00:00:46.496 --> 00:00:50.640
Increasing social support for&nbsp;
our most affected residents

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:55.520
And accelerating our capital works programme&nbsp;
by taking advantage of the Government’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.492
shovel ready and stimulus funding.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.451
We will also continue to seek support and funding from central government.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:11.840
Visit waimakariri.govt.nz/letstalk&nbsp;
to find out more.

